/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ONE CASE, TWO MODES (DEV.md 4c C152).  This case carries BOTH
  system/flowsheetDict (Process mode, choupoSolve) and system/propsDict
  (Properties & data mode, choupoProps) over ONE constant/.

  `application` names the DEFAULT mode -- what `runCase <case>` runs.  The
  other mode is one word away:
      runCase <case>            Process mode: the spiral-wound stage
      runCase <case> props      Properties & data mode: the membrane fit
      runCase <case> process    Process mode, said explicitly
  Information flows ONE way: Properties mode WRITES
  constant/assets/NF270_FdL2021.dat, Process mode only READS it -- and
  refuses it, naming the remedy, if its datasets or its fit block have
  changed since it was written.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
application   choupoSolve;
description   "One case, two modes: NF270's DSPM-DE pore fitted to published intrinsic rejections (Properties mode), then the fitted membrane in a spiral-wound stage (Process mode)";
verbosity     3;
